  "rationale": "The Linux build job repeatedly fetches and compiles Rust dependencies (cargo build --release --locked) inside a Debian container with no dependency cache, while the macOS job already uses rust-cache and the publish job already caches Maven. Adding a lockfile-keyed actions/cache step for the cargo registry (dependency download state only, not build outputs) before the build matches the P-LIT-GHA-CACHE dependency-caching experiments, which show reduced dependency-fetch time. The cache key includes runner.os, matrix.arch, and hashFiles('java/lance-jni/Cargo.lock'), so dependency changes invalidate it; CARGO_HOME is pointed at a workspace-mounted path so the container reuses the cached registry. No permissions are weakened, no new secrets, network, publishing, or deployment steps are added, and all existing build/test steps and coverage are preserved.",
